 Choices: A) Patients will spend more money on Heartaid, even though it is actually not any more effective than the current medication., B) Doctors will begin to prescribe Heartaid to patients, even though it is actually not any more effective than the current medication., C) Patients will continue to use the current medication, even though Heartaid is actually more effective., D) Researchers will calculate the wrong P-value, making their advice to doctors invalid.
